<section class="section tab-panel" id="height" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-height" hidden>
    <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Diagram 3</p>
            <h2>Height, light, paired fans, and risers</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
            <label for="light-clearance">Light clearance</label>
            <select id="light-clearance">
                <option value="20">20 inches · historical</option>
                <option value="18" selected>
                    18 inches · last recorded
                </option>
            </select>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="diagram-shell">
        <div class="diagram-header">
            <strong>Long-axis side elevation</strong>
            <span>
                Window at left · room at right · measure from the highest cactus/succulent tip in
                the light footprint
            </span>
        </div>
        <div class="height-grid">
            <svg
                class="diagram"
                viewBox="0 0 760 620"
                role="img"
                aria-labelledby="height-title height-desc"
            >
                <title id="height-title">
                                Long-axis elevation of the end-to-end grow
                                layout
                            </title>
                <desc id="height-desc">
                    Viewed from the divider toward the white wall, the window is on the left and the
                    room is on the right. The round glass table is at the window end and two wooden
                    tables are beyond it toward the room. All three tabletops are eighteen inches
                    from the floor. The tallest shared cactus is about twelve and one-half to
                    thirteen inches above the glass, while starter tips begin about four to seven
                    inches above the wood before risers. The August additions have not yet been
                    measured and remain directly on the second wood table. Six Mountain Crest plants
                    ordered August twenty-fifth are not shown because they have not arrived or been
                    measured. The fixture is currently forty-five percent at eighteen inches. Two
                    fan symbols at the window end represent vertically offset pole mounts, not exact
                    measured hub heights.
                </desc>

                <text x="74" y="24" class="svg-small">
                    WINDOW END · ROUND TABLE / FANS
                </text>
                <text x="686" y="24" class="svg-small" text-anchor="end">
                    ROOM END · TWO WOODEN TABLES
                </text>

                <rect x="185" y="46" width="390" height="34" rx="6" class="light"></rect>
                <line x1="245" y1="0" x2="245" y2="46" class="table-leg"></line>
                <line x1="515" y1="0" x2="515" y2="46" class="table-leg"></line>
                <text x="380" y="69" class="svg-label" text-anchor="middle">
                    AW200SE
                </text>
                <text x="380" y="102" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    AUGUST · 45% · 18 IN LED-TO-TIP
                </text>

                <line x1="76" y1="580" x2="684" y2="580" class="wall"></line>

                <rect x="100" y="400" width="285" height="24" rx="5" class="glass"></rect>
                <line x1="145" y1="424" x2="127" y2="580" class="table-leg"></line>
                <line x1="340" y1="424" x2="358" y2="580" class="table-leg"></line>
                <text x="242" y="449" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    ROUND TABLE · 18 IN HIGH
                </text>

                <rect x="430" y="400" width="230" height="24" rx="4" class="wood"></rect>
                <line x1="465" y1="424" x2="450" y2="580" class="table-leg"></line>
                <line x1="625" y1="424" x2="640" y2="580" class="table-leg"></line>
                <text x="545" y="449" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    TWO WOOD TABLES · 18 IN HIGH
                </text>

                <ellipse cx="242" cy="380" rx="82" ry="18" class="older-planter"></ellipse>
                <path d="M165 380L179 400H305L319 380Z" class="older-planter"></path>
                <rect x="229" y="270" width="26" height="110" rx="13" class="older-planter"></rect>
                <path d="M207 300C187 328 179 352 188 379" class="tail"></path>
                <text x="242" y="235" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    TALLEST SHARED: 12.5–13 IN
                </text>

                <path d="M445 400L452 382H490L497 400Z" class="pot"></path>
                <rect x="463" y="335" width="16" height="47" rx="8" class="older-planter"></rect>
                <text x="471" y="325" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    DIRECT
                </text>

                <rect
                    x="515"
                    y="361"
                    width="88"
                    height="39"
                    rx="5"
                    class="riser-lane riser-lane--permanent"
                ></rect>
                <path d="M529 361L536 344H578L585 361Z" class="pot"></path>
                <rect x="551" y="293" width="16" height="51" rx="8" class="older-planter"></rect>

                <rect
                    x="602"
                    y="388"
                    width="48"
                    height="12"
                    rx="4"
                    class="riser-lane riser-lane--permanent"
                ></rect>
                <path d="M599 388L606 371H644L651 388Z" class="pot"></path>
                <rect x="617" y="300" width="16" height="71" rx="8" class="older-planter"></rect>
                <text x="545" y="467" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    4–7 IN STARTER BAND + RISERS
                </text>
                <text x="545" y="486" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    AUGUST ADDITIONS: DIRECT UNTIL MEASURED
                </text>

                <line x1="105" y1="270" x2="660" y2="270" class="target"></line>
                <text x="380" y="258" class="svg-small" text-anchor="middle">
                    HIGHEST LIT CACTUS / SUCCULENT REFERENCE
                </text>

                <line x1="690" y1="80" x2="690" y2="270" class="measure"></line>
                <line x1="680" y1="80" x2="700" y2="80" class="measure"></line>
                <line x1="680" y1="270" x2="700" y2="270" class="measure"></line>
                <text
                    x="714"
                    y="180"
                    class="svg-label"
                    text-anchor="middle"
                    transform="rotate(90 714 180)"
                >
                    <tspan data-clearance>18</tspan>
                    IN LIGHT-TO-TIP
                </text>

                <line x1="78" y1="400" x2="78" y2="580" class="measure"></line>
                <line x1="68" y1="400" x2="88" y2="400" class="measure"></line>
                <line x1="68" y1="580" x2="88" y2="580" class="measure"></line>
                <text
                    x="54"
                    y="495"
                    class="svg-label"
                    text-anchor="middle"
                    transform="rotate(-90 54 495)"
                >
                    18 IN TABLE SURFACE
                </text>

                <circle cx="65" cy="190" r="27" class="fan"></circle>
                <path
                    d="M65 166Q84 190 65 214Q46 190 65 166M41 190Q65 171 89 190Q65 209 41 190"
                    class="fan-blade"
                ></path>
                <circle cx="65" cy="255" r="27" class="fan"></circle>
                <path
                    d="M65 231Q84 255 65 279Q46 255 65 231M41 255Q65 236 89 255Q65 274 41 255"
                    class="fan-blade"
                ></path>
                <line x1="65" y1="282" x2="65" y2="300" class="measure"></line>
                <text x="107" y="205" class="svg-small">
                    2× FAN HUBS
                </text>
                <text x="107" y="223" class="svg-small">
                    OFFSET · EXACT HEIGHTS PENDING
                </text>

                <text x="380" y="610" class="svg-label" text-anchor="middle">
                    VIEWED FROM DIVIDER TOWARD WHITE WALL · WINDOW LEFT / ROOM RIGHT
                </text>
            </svg>

            <aside class="measurement-panel">
                <h3>Tape-photo measurements</h3>
                <div class="measurement-grid">
                    <div class="field">
                        <label for="target-canopy">Target starter canopy above wood</label>
                        <input id="target-canopy" type="number" min="0" step="0.25" value="8.5" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="field">
                        <label for="sample-tip">Selected tip above wood</label>
                        <input id="sample-tip" type="number" min="0" step="0.25" value="5.5" />
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="result" aria-live="polite">
                    <strong id="riser-result">Calculating from the recorded measurements.</strong>
                    <span id="riser-detail">
                        The calculator will choose the available lift that places the selected tip
                        closest to the target starter canopy.
                    </span>
                </div>
                <div class="layout-note">
                    <p>
                        Use 8.5 inches as a starting canopy height and adjust each pot for its light
                        needs. Enter a fresh tabletop-to-tip measurement. Keep A1 lower at the outer
                        edge if its pale tissue reacts, and keep both shared planters directly on
                        the table.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="riser-inventory" aria-label="Available acrylic riser sizes">
        <div class="riser">
            <strong>+1.18 in</strong>
            <span>7.87 × 2.95-inch top</span>
        </div>
        <div class="riser">
            <strong>+2.75 in</strong>
            <span>8.26 × 2.95-inch top</span>
        </div>
        <div class="riser">
            <strong>+3.93 in</strong>
            <span>8.66 × 2.95-inch top</span>
        </div>
        <div class="riser">
            <strong>+5.11 in</strong>
            <span>9.05 × 2.95-inch top</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="layout-note">
        <p>
            Install one riser left-to-right beneath the two center-side pots in each physical row,
            as shown above. This is a photo-derived starting plan: A3/B1 use +5.11, D3/A2 use +3.93,
            D2/C3 use +2.75, and B2/C2 use +1.18. A1, C1, D1, and B3 stay direct. Because every
            acrylic top is only 2.95 inches wide, dry-fit the attached saucers before trusting a
            two-pot shelf. Three pots will not fit safely. Use one pot per riser or leave the row
            direct if either pot rocks, tips, or slides; never stack the stands.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
